# ============================================================
# ONE-STOP CHUNK (UPDATED): Descriptive source-fingerprint analyses
# for 17 persistent hotspot groups
#
# Produces:
#   1) "Power figure" (6 panels): Map (labeled) + Chemical fingerprint +
#      TRI distance + Persistence + Ratio heatmap + Hour-of-day activity heatmap
#   2) Per-hotspot wind-resolved CPF:
#        - uses GLOBAL thresholds (p95 by default)
#        - falls back to percentile=75 if threshold mode fails
#        - also saves mean polar plots
#   3) Per-hotspot pollutant-ratio summaries (T/B, X/B, TMB/B, H2S/B, HCN/B)
#   4) Per-hotspot local map (NO TRI), pairwise scatter panel, polarPlot (nwr),
#      and hour-of-day plots
#   5) Saves tidy descriptive outputs:
#        - hotspot_ratio_summary_ALL.csv + per-group ratio CSVs
#        - hotspot_hour_activity_ALL.csv
#        - hotspot_master_with_source_flags.csv
#        - hotspot_descriptive_summary.csv
#        - optional ratio-space scatterplot (NO clustering)
#
# INPUTS:
#   - MASTER_hotspot_group_index.csv (updated with TRI columns)
#   - mobile_wswd.RData (df or out with Longitude/Latitude/date/ws/wd + pollutant cols)
#
# BASEMAP:
#   - Uses ggspatial::annotation_map_tile(type="cartolight", zoom=...)
#   - Does NOT plot TRI facilities on hotspot maps
# ============================================================

